| `-FullComment 0x326f5d20 <line:34:3, line:62:18>
|   |-ParagraphComment 0x326f5870 <line:34:3, line:36:23>
|   | |-TextComment 0x326f57f0 <line:34:3, col:96> Text=" SkSpan holds a reference to contiguous data of type T along with a count. SkSpan does not own"
|   | |-TextComment 0x326f5810 <line:35:3, col:95> Text=" the data itself but is merely a reference, therefore you must take care with the lifetime of"
|   | `-TextComment 0x326f5830 <line:36:3, col:23> Text=" the underlying data."
|   |-ParagraphComment 0x326f5910 <line:38:3, line:40:15>
|   | |-TextComment 0x326f5890 <line:38:3, col:91> Text=" SkSpan is a count and a pointer into existing array or data type that stores its data in"
|   | |-TextComment 0x326f58b0 <line:39:3, col:96> Text=" contiguous memory like std::vector. Any container that works with std::size() and std::data()"
|   | `-TextComment 0x326f58d0 <line:40:3, col:15> Text=" can be used."
|   |-ParagraphComment 0x326f5980 <line:42:3, line:43:73>
|   | |-TextComment 0x326f5930 <line:42:3, col:100> Text=" SkSpan makes a convenient parameter for a routine to accept array like things. This allows you to"
|   | `-TextComment 0x326f5950 <line:43:3, col:73> Text=" write the routine without overloads for all different container types."
|   |-ParagraphComment 0x326f5a40 <line:45:3, line:46:48>
|   | |-TextComment 0x326f59a0 <line:45:3, col:11> Text=" Example:"
|   | |-TextComment 0x326f59c0 <line:46:3, col:26> Text="     void routine(SkSpan"
|   | |-TextComment 0x326f59e0 <col:27, col:32> Text="<const"
|   | `-TextComment 0x326f5a00 <col:33, col:48> Text=" int> a) { ... }"
|   |-ParagraphComment 0x326f5a90 <line:48:3, col:39>
|   | `-TextComment 0x326f5a60 <col:3, col:39> Text="     std::vector v = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};"
|   |-ParagraphComment 0x326f5ae0 <line:50:3, col:18>
|   | `-TextComment 0x326f5ab0 <col:3, col:18> Text="     routine(a);"
|   |-ParagraphComment 0x326f5b50 <line:52:3, line:53:71>
|   | |-TextComment 0x326f5b00 <line:52:3, col:98> Text=" A word of caution when working with initializer_list, initializer_lists have a lifetime that is"
